Netcatty
  https://github.com/binaricat/Netcatty
  Copyright (C) binaricat and Netcatty contributors
  License: GPL-3.0-or-later

  Parts of the Z-SSH user interface (base UI components, theme tokens and
  presets, terminal themes, title bar, host vault views, settings page,
  terminal layer, server stats bar, AI chat side panel) and the server
  stats collection script were adapted from Netcatty. The in-terminal AI
  command execution logic (crates/zssh-core/src/ai/pty.rs command wrapper,
  end-marker parsing and output normalization, ported from
  electron/bridges/ai/ptyExec.cjs and ptyExecHelpers.cjs), the remote
  login-shell probe (crates/zssh-core/src/ai/shell_kind.rs, ported from
  electron/bridges/ai/sessionShellKind.cjs and lib/localShellRules.json;
  POSIX probe branch only) and the terminal display filter
  (crates/zssh-core/src/ai/display.rs, ported from electron/preload.cjs
  filterMcpChunk / flushMcpBufferedOutput and electron/bridges/ai/shellUtils.cjs
  formatSyntheticEcho) were also adapted
  from Netcatty. The codex agent driver
  (crates/zssh-core/src/ai/agent/codex/, JSON-RPC handshake and shared
  process lifecycle, approval decision mapping and event translation,
  adapted from electron/bridges/aiBridge/codexAppServer/connection.cjs and
  runtime.cjs and electron/bridges/aiBridge/sdk/codexDriver.cjs) was also
  adapted from Netcatty. The Claude Code agent driver
  (crates/zssh-core/src/ai/agent/claude/, stream-json session handling and
  event translation, session resume after the process is closed, adapted
  from electron/bridges/aiBridge/sdk/claudeDriver.cjs) was also
  adapted from Netcatty. The SFTP/transfer engine
  (crates/zssh-core/src/sftp/: staging `.part` files, resume with a
  verification read on both sides, pause/resume, conflict handling and the
  list of local-vs-remote edge cases) references
  electron/bridges/sftpBridge.cjs and transferBridge.cjs for the problem
  space and boundary cases; it is an independent Rust implementation, not a
  code port. The SFTP dual-pane user interface
  (ui/src/components/sftp/: the file pane with breadcrumb, filter, sorting
  and virtual list, the tab view with the transfer queue and context menu,
  and the conflict / permissions / name / delete dialogs, plus the sorting,
  filtering and selection logic in ui/src/state/sftpPane.ts and the data
  shapes in ui/src/api/sftp.ts) was adapted from Netcatty
  components/sftp/ (SftpPaneFileList, SftpPaneToolbar, SftpBreadcrumb,
  SftpPaneView, SftpTransferQueue, SftpTransferItem, SftpConflictDialog,
  SftpPermissionsDialog, sftpSorting); the layout, the option semantics and
  the dialogs were followed, while the code was rewritten against the Z-SSH
  data model and Tauri commands. The SFTP panel docked next to the terminal
  (ui/src/components/sftp/SftpDockPanel.tsx, adapted from
  components/SftpSidePanel.tsx) and the "follow the terminal's directory"
  probe (crates/zssh-core/src/ssh/cwd.rs: the POSIX sh script that finds the
  user's PTY shell as a sibling process of the exec channel, follows the
  foreground shell chain and reads /proc/<pid>/cwd, ported and simplified
  from electron/bridges/sshBridge/sessionOps.cjs getSessionPwd) were also
  adapted from Netcatty. The configuration-sync settings page
  (ui/src/components/settings/sync/: connection form, master password
  setup, sync status, conflict list and local backups, plus the status
  bar in ui/src/components/sync/) follows the layout and wording of
  components/cloud-sync/ (CloudSyncControls, CloudSyncDashboardTabs,
  CloudSyncDialogs, CloudSyncLocalBackupsPanel); the sync engine, the
  encryption and the WebDAV / S3 storages are independent Rust
  implementations. The OneDrive storage (crates/zssh-core/src/sync/onedrive/)
  follows the OAuth scope set, the refresh-failure error classification and
  the app-folder (special/approot) addressing of
  electron/bridges/onedriveAuthBridge.cjs and
  infrastructure/services/adapters/OneDriveAdapter.ts; the PKCE loopback
  listener, the conditional (eTag / If-Match) upload-session writes and
  everything else there are independent Rust implementations. Adapted files are marked with an "Adapted
  from Netcatty" comment at the top. The Z-SSH
  backend (SSH, flow control, vault storage, authentication, proxy and
  jump-host dialing, connection pool, AI tool bridge, opencode / codex /
  claude agent drivers) is an independent Rust implementation.
  The host operating-system logos and brand colours (ui/src/assets/os/,
  ui/src/components/vault/OsIcon.tsx) and the os-release name matching in
  crates/zssh-core/src/ssh/os_probe.rs were adapted from Netcatty
  public/distro/, components/DistroAvatar.tsx and domain/host.ts. The
  logos are trademarks of their respective owners.

